{{#is_recovery}}Buffer write duration recovered for `{{component_id.name}}` in pipeline `{{pipeline_name.name}}`.{{/is_recovery}}

## Which component_id matters
This metric is "duration spent sending a payload to this buffer", so each series is the time spent writing *into* the named component, not the time that component spends working. On a topology where a processor group wraps one or more processors, those are different boundaries:

- The **group** is addressed as a topology node: the source writes into it and the destination reads from it. Its value is the queue the source actually blocks on, and it will match the source's blocked time closely.
- A **processor inside the group** is fed by the group's own dispatcher, one batch at a time, so it almost never waits. A reading in single-digit milliseconds there is normal and is not evidence that the stage is healthy.

Alert on the group. During a sustained stall the inner processor can read in milliseconds while the group reads in seconds, so the inner row alone will tell you nothing is wrong.

